# Punctuation: hyphen, not em dash

In **UI copy** (Streamlit labels, captions, banners, empty states, chart labels, alerts) and **README** text, never use the em dash character `—` (U+2014).

Use a plain hyphen-minus instead: `-`

## Examples

- Good: `InsightAI - Complaint Intelligence Platform`
- Bad: `InsightAI — Complaint Intelligence Platform`
- Good: `Billing (14) - 29.2%`
- Bad: `Billing (14) — 29.2%`
- Good: empty/missing values shown as `-`
- Bad: empty/missing values shown as `—`

Code comments outside UI/README may keep either style; prefer `-` for consistency when editing nearby.
